  ('2874a9ba42f514480630c73d63102b87fd5570c8f591f556b0e911d712ef2519', 'ず is the Old Japanese negative, the same one in ざるを得ない and にかかわらず, carried inside an otherwise modern frame: いられない is the potential negative of いる, which the classical language did not form this way.

