  ('2d277d4200eae087a79ffab5f54803df290a62fca08e376beb1cf466c004e754', '堪える yields both readings of the pattern: unbearable to, and unable to contain.', '[{"t":"堪","r":"こら"},{"t":"える"},{"t":" yields both readings of the pattern: unbearable to, and unable to contain."}]'::jsonb),
  ('7a49dd26c0eb444d5b942e5976cbda8f282c82ad5be750792a48d109a98ac1d4', '見るに堪えない is unbearable to watch; 感謝に堪えない is being unable to contain gratitude. One verb, and what decides which you get is the noun in front rather than anything in the ending.

