  ('19f6d262d1ab1a4e31231aba6c9ad4373b10a37ae4236cb20cd3e7836359dd8e', 'なし is the Old Japanese adjective behind modern ない. なしに alone simply means without; adding は marks that absence as the topic and sets up a denial about it.

