  ('9d72291e0183523052d394f253c32696a93a998a0c0c484b0988ce9ba736d66d', 'The て of the te-form is the old perfective つ, which linked one action to the next without stating when either happened. Only the final verb carries tense, which is why 起きて、食べて、行きました is entirely past.

