  ('518f5fa261dcc5b874df95bcdeeffd10ca8f0e0dffb399e3d2b1ecfa833aab3f', 'なさる is the respectful form of する, and its imperative is なさい. So the form is polite in origin, which is why it lands as firm rather than rude.

