  ('aa2e87bee235189a1917bc3c69d99f351285f1ed111906334fb66e74dfd3ea32', 'じょうず is a genuine Sino-Japanese compound, the upper hand. へた is not its mirror: it is a native word, most likely 端 (はた), the shallow edge rather than the deep part, and 下手 was written onto it later to make the pair look symmetrical.

