  ('5c5ac7f3c64e9eb8c3ae986d56f67060a77c6f30e62cd8112d408f7eb5100886', 'The names 五段 and 一段 say exactly what the verbs do: move through five vowel rows, or stay on one.', '[{"t":"The names "},{"t":"五","r":"うー"},{"t":"段","r":"だん"},{"t":" and "},{"t":"一","r":"いっち"},{"t":"段","r":"だん"},{"t":" say exactly what the verbs do: move through five vowel rows, or stay on one."}]'::jsonb),
  ('7d9cd96f7f2f36e40933b73415dc8475c8eb2d113566281f30cca12b0ab0e440', '書く runs across か・き・く・け・こ: five steps, 五段. 食べる never leaves the え row: 食べない, 食べます, 食べる, 食べれば. One step, 一段. The fifth step is newer than it looks: the class was called 四段 until the 1946 kana reform respelled 書かう as 書こう and added the お row.

So the classification is not a list to memorise but a description of the stem you can watch happening. It also explains why only 五段 verbs have a て-form worth learning rules for: a stem that moves has consonants colliding with the ending, and a stem that stays put does not.', '[{"t":"書","r":"か"},{"t":"く"},{"t":" runs across "},{"t":"か・き・く・け・こ"},{"t":": five steps, "},{"t":"五","r":"うー"},{"t":"段","r":"だん"},{"t":". "},{"t":"食","r":"た"},{"t":"べる"},{"t":" never leaves the "},{"t":"え"},{"t":" row: "},{"t":"食","r":"た"},{"t":"べない"},{"t":", "},{"t":"食","r":"た"},{"t":"べます"},{"t":", "},{"t":"食","r":"た"},{"t":"べる"},{"t":", "},{"t":"食","r":"た"},{"t":"べれば"},{"t":". One step, "},{"t":"一","r":"いっち"},{"t":"段","r":"だん"},{"t":". The fifth step is newer than it looks: the class was called "},{"t":"四","r":"し"},{"t":"段","r":"だん"},{"t":" until the 1946 kana reform respelled "},{"t":"書","r":"か"},{"t":"かう"},{"t":" as "},{"t":"書","r":"か"},{"t":"こう"},{"t":" and added the "},{"t":"お"},{"t":" row.\n\nSo the classification is not a list to memorise but a description of the stem you can watch happening. It also explains why only "},{"t":"五","r":"うー"},{"t":"段","r":"だん"},{"t":" verbs have a "},{"t":"て"},{"t":"-form worth learning rules for: a stem that moves has consonants colliding with the ending, and a stem that stays put does not."}]'::jsonb),
  ('6349428dab5bc0dd15b08577db4608fbfed91a977bb726b6b306fd4d18262447', '本か雑誌 leaves both open rather than choosing. It is the same か that turns 誰 into 誰か and a statement into a question.

