  ('6204efe39bb099507fa3a0f3cacf4faf6e88c465e0cf7022e638d27263e8068b', '好き is not a verb. It is a な-adjective, and that is why the thing liked takes が.', '[{"t":"好","r":"ず"},{"t":"き"},{"t":" is not a verb. It is a "},{"t":"な"},{"t":"-adjective, and that is why the thing liked takes "},{"t":"が"},{"t":"."}]'::jsonb),
  ('183e110b3e824d650e8a1cb4cbd52fb4b47f572e9ada81445f8231aa0330fa43', '音楽が好きです says the music is likeable-to-me. There is no verb "to like" in the sentence, so there is no object, so を would have nothing to mark.

