  ('c283c0318465afc93ec3ec64b7926bd83b0e805bef95541b2d6e10a336e5d885', 'あげく is 挙句, the closing verse of a linked-verse poem.', '[{"t":"あげく"},{"t":" is "},{"t":"挙","r":"あ"},{"t":"句","r":"く"},{"t":", the closing verse of a linked-verse poem."}]'::jsonb),
  ('714ab7b1fbe176c707055de8ea64eaaa8b8d9190efcdc6518c03815da5efe07b', '連歌 was composed in sequence by several poets, and the 挙句 was the last verse, the one everything before had been building toward. The phrase 挙句の果て still carries that finality.

