  ('1bbf8cce59961d4111b6658d2b5ae2814b888a5b3398714a2ae7afd444cc8282', 'べく is the 連用形 of べし, the form that connects onward to a verb.', '[{"t":"べく"},{"t":" is the "},{"t":"連","r":"つ"},{"t":"用","r":"よう"},{"t":"形","r":"なり"},{"t":" of "},{"t":"べし"},{"t":", the form that connects onward to a verb."}]'::jsonb),
  ('4f3459205ab1e7911ab92ee65db9d14d13705c6ac24cb952cc05b83234441f51', 'べし had a full classical paradigm. べき modified nouns, べく linked to what followed, and べからず negated it. All three survive, each in its own modern niche.

