  ('c40ec94b7ccc9715391ca86337877bf9971fab8202a7a18fb072831a8f842f2b', 'わけ is 分け, from 分ける "to divide", a distinction drawn, hence the sense a thing makes.', '[{"t":"わけ"},{"t":" is "},{"t":"分","r":"わ"},{"t":"け"},{"t":", from "},{"t":"分","r":"わ"},{"t":"ける"},{"t":" \"to divide\", a distinction drawn, hence the sense a thing makes."}]'::jsonb),
  ('1f69e56ca12f32dd1f676b53d2a11c2a9fe5c2bdc678a86999bbb8836e3293a4', '訳 is only its customary spelling; the on-reading やく, "translate", has nothing to do with it. The word is the nominalised 分け, and it shares its root with 分かる: something divided off is something told apart, and what you can tell apart makes sense. 訳が分からない contains the same idea twice.

わけだ says a reason for this exists and has just become apparent, which is why it lands as "no wonder" rather than as a fresh claim.

The whole family is that noun with different endings attached. わけがない denies the reason exists at all; わけではない denies only that this is the reason; わけにはいかない says the reason cannot be made to go anywhere. Learn the noun and the three patterns stop being separate items.', '[{"t":"訳","r":"わけ"},{"t":" is only its customary spelling; the on-reading "},{"t":"やく"},{"t":", \"translate\", has nothing to do with it. The word is the nominalised "},{"t":"分","r":"わ"},{"t":"け"},{"t":", and it shares its root with "},{"t":"分","r":"わ"},{"t":"かる"},{"t":": something divided off is something told apart, and what you can tell apart makes sense. "},{"t":"訳","r":"わけ"},{"t":"が"},{"t":"分","r":"わ"},{"t":"からない"},{"t":" contains the same idea twice.\n\n"},{"t":"わけだ"},{"t":" says a reason for this exists and has just become apparent, which is why it lands as \"no wonder\" rather than as a fresh claim.\n\nThe whole family is that noun with different endings attached. "},{"t":"わけがない"},{"t":" denies the reason exists at all; "},{"t":"わけではない"},{"t":" denies only that this is the reason; "},{"t":"わけにはいかない"},{"t":" says the reason cannot be made to go anywhere. Learn the noun and the three patterns stop being separate items."}]'::jsonb),
  ('4df576e49a98c99abad2076184b71ef3098b29f090c878e77db85cb4d45de8a6', 'をはじめ is 始め, the noun from 始める, the head of a list, not merely its first item.', '[{"t":"をはじめ"},{"t":" is "},{"t":"始","r":"はじ"},{"t":"め"},{"t":", the noun from "},{"t":"始","r":"はじ"},{"t":"める"},{"t":", the head of a list, not merely its first item."}]'::jsonb),
  ('a3ea3a33005336bc0f75fb09f225cb12ccd0d4697f492542dd1dff719d0e345f', 'The 連用形 used as a noun, the same shape as 限り and 通り. What it names is the leading example, and the rest follow from it.

