  ('efff89740e74c94f77a02fbdd8f13c09568cbe202c933a09744f361b7341664d', '出る plus 来る. Before it meant "can", 出来る meant something was produced or came about, a sense still plain in 出来上がる and in 出来事, "an occurrence".

So 話すことができる says the speaking-of-it comes about. That is a whole noun phrase with a verb after it, not an ending on a verb, and it is why the construction is the formal one: it takes the long way round, naming the act before saying it is possible.', '[{"t":"出","r":"で"},{"t":"る"},{"t":" plus "},{"t":"来","r":"く"},{"t":"る"},{"t":". Before it meant \"can\", "},{"t":"出","r":"で"},{"t":"来","r":"く"},{"t":"る"},{"t":" meant something was produced or came about, a sense still plain in "},{"t":"出来上","r":"できあ"},{"t":"がる"},{"t":" and in "},{"t":"出来事","r":"できごと"},{"t":", \"an occurrence\".\n\nSo "},{"t":"話","r":"はな"},{"t":"すことができる"},{"t":" says the speaking-of-it comes about. That is a whole noun phrase with a verb after it, not an ending on a verb, and it is why the construction is the formal one: it takes the long way round, naming the act before saying it is possible."}]'::jsonb),
  ('e9e614ebc809ba175587d9a17241958d58ede5c1cf2e98ab84c513551c65191f', '出来る is 出る plus 来る, literally "to come out".', '[{"t":"出","r":"で"},{"t":"来","r":"く"},{"t":"る"},{"t":" is "},{"t":"出","r":"で"},{"t":"る"},{"t":" plus "},{"t":"来","r":"く"},{"t":"る"},{"t":", literally \"to come out\"."}]'::jsonb),
  ('dbfdbabf120c1deee13bc2a3460f2d42c2022bcb9c71717200e5bf2368ae3765', 'Before it meant "can", 出来る meant something came about or was produced, a sense still plain in 出来上がる and 出来事, "an occurrence".

