  ('ce17bf2c0ad0044de070a4e5fdc5c651a9301487e6202ec25619787b96f19f99', '皮切り is the first burn in a course of moxibustion, the one that cuts the skin.', '[{"t":"皮","r":"かわ"},{"t":"切","r":"き"},{"t":"り"},{"t":" is the first burn in a course of moxibustion, the one that cuts the skin."}]'::jsonb),
  ('048abb57ab591d34a495a69d03eacde0d7716649ef97e1caf73137b51565ab0b', 'Moxa was burned on the skin in a series, and the 皮切り was the opening application: the sharpest, and the one everything after followed from.

That is why the pattern is not merely "first" but first-and-then-spreading. 東京を皮切りに全国へ needs the expansion to follow; a first item with nothing after it is not a 皮切り, however first it was.', '[{"t":"Moxa was burned on the skin in a series, and the "},{"t":"皮","r":"かわ"},{"t":"切","r":"き"},{"t":"り"},{"t":" was the opening application: the sharpest, and the one everything after followed from.\n\nThat is why the pattern is not merely \"first\" but first-and-then-spreading. "},{"t":"東","r":"とん"},{"t":"京を"},{"t":"皮","r":"かわ"},{"t":"切","r":"き"},{"t":"りに"},{"t":"全国","r":"ぜんこく"},{"t":"へ"},{"t":" needs the expansion to follow; a first item with nothing after it is not a "},{"t":"皮","r":"かわ"},{"t":"切","r":"き"},{"t":"り"},{"t":", however first it was."}]'::jsonb),
  ('960c7acdde6addff3aa39eafd71b6d30a048ea8cb48ec3b9bf5aaa34a8b6615b', '相まって is 相 ("mutually") with 俟つ, two things relying on each other.', '[{"t":"相","r":"あい"},{"t":"まって"},{"t":" is "},{"t":"相","r":"あい"},{"t":" (\"mutually\") with "},{"t":"俟つ"},{"t":", two things relying on each other."}]'::jsonb),
  ('eea09cb3d0a53b529d42fe65b6e1d2962c8592c2275d4de76e98f5fbefed7fe2', '相 is the prefix in 相手 and 相談, marking something done between parties. The verb is 俟つ, "to await, to rely on" (not the plain 待つ it is often written as), so the image is two things each counting on the other.

That mutual sense is why と相まって needs both halves to contribute. It is not "along with" but "each amplified by the other", which is why the result named afterwards is always more than either alone.', '[{"t":"相","r":"あい"},{"t":" is the prefix in "},{"t":"相手","r":"あいて"},{"t":" and "},{"t":"相談","r":"そうだん"},{"t":", marking something done between parties. The verb is "},{"t":"俟つ"},{"t":", \"to await, to rely on\" (not the plain "},{"t":"待","r":"ま"},{"t":"つ"},{"t":" it is often written as), so the image is two things each counting on the other.\n\nThat mutual sense is why "},{"t":"と"},{"t":"相","r":"あい"},{"t":"まって"},{"t":" needs both halves to contribute. It is not \"along with\" but \"each amplified by the other\", which is why the result named afterwards is always more than either alone."}]'::jsonb),
  ('0815084bbb05975a72eb8a3a6b0e7a2e36e95e746f9d96cb8a1ffc3e17fd3129', '至り is from 至る, "to arrive", the point a thing has arrived at.', '[{"t":"至","r":"いた"},{"t":"り"},{"t":" is from "},{"t":"至","r":"いた"},{"t":"る"},{"t":", \"to arrive\", the point a thing has arrived at."}]'::jsonb),
  ('3b0a2a9c56df5ef1e51c65a93df134ecffe49f9e95d39356efc2f3098b7e214a', '至る is the verb on road signs, 東京に至る. 光栄の至り is honour arrived at its furthest.

It pairs with の極み as the two formal superlatives, and they differ by image rather than degree: 至り is where something got to, 極み is the top of it. Both belong to speeches and letters, and both take only abstract nouns.', '[{"t":"至","r":"いた"},{"t":"る"},{"t":" is the verb on road signs, "},{"t":"東","r":"とん"},{"t":"京に"},{"t":"至","r":"いた"},{"t":"る"},{"t":". "},{"t":"光","r":"ひかり"},{"t":"栄","r":"さか"},{"t":"の"},{"t":"至","r":"いた"},{"t":"り"},{"t":" is honour arrived at its furthest.\n\nIt pairs with "},{"t":"の"},{"t":"極","r":"ごく"},{"t":"み"},{"t":" as the two formal superlatives, and they differ by image rather than degree: "},{"t":"至","r":"いた"},{"t":"り"},{"t":" is where something got to, "},{"t":"極","r":"ごく"},{"t":"み"},{"t":" is the top of it. Both belong to speeches and letters, and both take only abstract nouns."}]'::jsonb),
  ('885cbfda8a571c534fe8bba2149a7eb8ce2c92feb24f546f0efc348c788df05a', '込める is "to put into, to load", the verb for charging something with contents.', '[{"t":"込","r":"こ"},{"t":"める"},{"t":" is \"to put into, to load\", the verb for charging something with contents."}]'::jsonb),
  ('ebece6c1d3a9613da99868d1de38c28926a54b03d6cef71806a1084c82ba7e65', '弾を込める is loading a round. 心を込めて is loading the feeling in, and the metaphor is as physical in Japanese as it sounds.

